<title>NETHERLANDS: TENNIS-HEINEKEN TROPHY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-HEINEKEN TROPHY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROSMALEN, Netherlands 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the Heineken Trophy tennis tournament on Thursday (prefix number denotes seed):</p>
<p>Men's second round:</p>
<p>3-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Hendrik Dreekmann</p>
<p>(Germany) 6-0 6-3</p>
<p>Martin Damm (Czech Republic) beat Chris Woodruff (U.S) 6-1 6-7</p>
<p>(3-7) 6-1</p>
<p>Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands) beat Leander Paes (India) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Guillaume Raoux (France) beat Karim Alami (Morocco) 6-4 2-6 7-6</p>
<p>(7-4)</p>
<p>Women's quarter finals:</p>
<p>1-Anke Huber (Germany) beat 5-Sabine Appelmans (Belgium) 6-2</p>
<p>4-6 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>8-Asa Carlsson (Sweden) beat 2-Mary Pierce (France), walkerover</p>
<p>(Pierce withdrew injured)</p>
<p>3-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania) beat 6-Dominique van Roost</p>
<p>(Belgium) 6-1 2-6 6-4</p>
<p>Miriam Oremans (Netherlands) beat 4-Karina Habsudova (Slovakia)</p>
<p>6-2 7-5</p>
</text>
